# Force www to apex domain. 301! = forced, so no existing file can shadow it.
http://www.burgonomics.com/*    http://burgonomics.com/:splat    301!
https://www.burgonomics.com/*   https://burgonomics.com/:splat   301!

# Old site pages -> new pages (keeps existing links and Google results working).
# Order matters: Netlify applies the FIRST matching rule, so these must stay
# above the SPA fallback.
/team        /about   301
/team.html   /about   301
/menu.html   /menu    301

# Legacy .html pages this project's own static build published: its nav linked
# to ./about.html, ./locations.html and ./franchise.html (see commit 555bc39,
# the pre-React site whose ./menu.html is still live). Safe if the old host
# never served them - the visitor still lands on the matching new page.
/about.html      /about       301
/locations.html  /locations   301
/franchise.html  /franchise   301

# SPA fallback for the React routes (/, /menu, /locations, /franchise, /about)
# and unknown paths. Deliberately NOT forced: Netlify serves an existing static
# file before applying a non-forced rule (shadowing), so /assets/*, /fonts/*,
# /frames/*, /menu_images/*, /team_images/* and /favicon.svg still reach the
# filesystem instead of this rewrite.
/*               /index.html  200
